{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320399-conceptual-relationship-is-it-sympahty-if-not-what-can-it-be","id":1320399,"title":"Conceptual relationship, is it Sympahty? If not what can it be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-23T21:27:06-07:00","id":1320399,"title":"Conceptual relationship, is it Sympahty? If not what can it be?","content":"Reading through the Question thread I fall upon the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do memories have sympathetic ties to their subjects?<br /> Like if a guy had a memory of a small town in Connecticut,<br /> or a chick had a fond memory of a music box their friend once owned.<br /> Do these memories hold ties to their subjects, or is it just the owners of these memories that have the ties? </div> </div> </div>To which the answer was<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Memories granting sympathetic connections to anyone but the person that created them would have setting-changing effects. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might be able to turn them into a Sympathetic Representation Yantra, but you'd need to have them out of your head to do so, and you would still need Sympathy to the subject you want to effect. Other than that, no, because those are the memories of the person who created them, no one else's, and under normal circumstances no one else even has access to them. </div> </div> </div>I thought that since Sympathy can connect stuff through Conceptual Relationship (lines/threads connecting them through Space), it might be able to connect them through Mind (lines/threads connecting things through memories, then through Oneiros, then through the various layers of the Astral). I can accept that since, say, Abraham Lincoln has/had a different version in life, as ghost, my memory, my Oneiros and the &quot;idea of Lincoln&quot; in the Temenos, it must mean that they are all different &quot;entities&quot;.<br /> <br /> But shouldn't they have some metaphysical connection (setting-wise) since they are related? If not Space, what kind of Supernal Magic (besides Legacies) would be able to reveal to me for example &quot;All stuff related to Lincoln&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T22:34:11-07:00","id":1320410,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends entirely on the medium. Within a computer? Forces. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1318227#post1318227\">Within a book</a> or someone's head? Mind. Spirits related to him? You get the gist.<br /> <br /> But abstractly? Metaphysically? It may be nothing could do that. There are gaps within the arcana and the practices. They're not infallible. They can do almost anything, but not everything.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to see the feedback of others though, some of the people here have some pretty nifty ideas and understanding in regards to magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 06-24-2019, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T03:49:03-07:00","id":1320448,"title":"","content":"Sympathy would be the mechanism by which all variations of Lincoln are associated, but that doesn\u2019t mean that the connections would be powerful enough to be of use in magic as more than a Representation Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T04:10:16-07:00","id":1320452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1320399-conceptual-relationship-is-it-sympahty-if-not-what-can-it-be#post1320399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But shouldn't they have some metaphysical connection (setting-wise) since they are related? If not Space, what kind of Supernal Magic (besides Legacies) would be able to reveal to me for example &quot;All stuff related to Lincoln&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate.<br /> <br /> It's still sympathy enough for it to work as Sympathetic Yantras (which is a Space thing) but with only symbolism to go on only Fate would be able to do anything, and mostly you point you in the direction of things you want based on this symbolism (so Fate mostly just does what it could already do).<br /> Also, the symbolic connections might make it easier to pass from &quot;related&quot; Astral realms representing the subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":